WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.560
App dev, Analytics, Security,
and so much more on This Week

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.550
In Cloud, where we bring
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:08.460
Google Cloud Next
was crazy this year

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.140
with lots of announcements,
so let's get started.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.410
First up, the latest
launch is in App dev.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.060
Anthos was launched,
which helps you

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.490
span across hybrid or
multi-cloud environments

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:18.840
with your services.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.990
Using Kubernetes through Google
Kubernetes Engine and GKE

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.760
On-Prem, you'll
have a standard way

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.660
to deploy services with built-in
policy and security automation,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.610
plus unified monitoring.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.430
And to help support automation
across hybrid workloads,

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.230
Cloud Run was also
announced, which

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.840
enables developers to
run serverless containers

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.480
in a fully-managed fashion on
GCP, on GKE, or on premises.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.440
In the world of
databases and analytics,

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.180
one of our most
exciting announcements

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.520
was BigQuery BI
Engine, which allows

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.820
you to do first-class BI in
Data Studio, our dashboarding

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.290
and reporting tool.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.930
You can now use a super-fast
in-memory analysis service

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.480
for BigQuery to analyze
large and complex data

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.720
sets interactively, all with
sub-second query response

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.580
time and high concurrency.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.440
Analysts can perform
speed-of-thought data

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:07.620
exploration on their latest
data via Data Studio and Google

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:08.910
Sheets.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:10.710
Plus, Cloud SQL
just added support

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.240
for a new database type--

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.700
Managed SQL Server, a
fully-managed service

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:18.070
for SQL Server but with built-in
performance, scalability,

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:20.970
and security so you can
focus on your applications.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.310
On the data management
front, our Data Fusion launch

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.860
provides a fully-managed,
code-free data integration

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.520
service that helps you
move data and then process

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.863
and land that data within GCP.

00:01:30.863 --> 00:01:33.030
And we can't forget about
the exciting announcements

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.350
in machine learning.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:36.120
AutoML tables was
launched, which

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.010
enables you to
automatically build models

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:42.150
on arbitrary tables of data,
like BigQuery tables or CSV.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:44.640
Now, data scientists,
analysts, and developers

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.183
can automatically
build and deploy

00:01:46.183 --> 00:01:47.850
state of the art
machine-learning models

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:50.460
on structured data at a
massively increased speed

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.110
and scale.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:55.020
We've also announced incredible
launches in security.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.580
Our Cloud Security
Command Center

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:59.430
went GA a single
centralized dashboard

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:03.510
that helps security teams gather
data, identify threats, and act

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:06.462
on them before they result
in business damage or loss.

00:02:06.462 --> 00:02:07.920
And with event
threat detection, it

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.220
can detect suspicious
activity from Stackdriver logs

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.500
and then flags them
for remediation.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.907
The threats will be surface in
Cloud Security Command Center.

00:02:16.907 --> 00:02:18.990
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:21.120
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.320
Have thoughts or ideas?

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.950
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.390
We'll see you in the Cloud.

